   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch6/q2",
   "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x^2+9}}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Using a substitution, that should be stated clearly, show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\mathrm f(x)\\,\\mathrm dx=A\\sinh^{-1}(Bx)+c\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> is an arbitrary constant and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence find, in exact form in terms of natural logarithms, the mean value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> over the interval <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[0,3]\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
